<<<
Grecian)(Greek. The first is now curiously restricted by idiom to architecture, facial outline, the Grecian bend & knot, & Grecian slippers. We seldom talk of Grecian, but usually of Greek, history, fire, calends, lyrics, tyrants, Church, dialects, aspirations, though Grecian noses & brows, colonnades & pediments, may still be heard of.
===
**Grecian)(Greek.** The first is now curiously restricted by idiom to architecture, facial outline, the *Grecian bend* & *knot*, & *Grecian slippers*. We seldom talk of *Grecian*, but usually of *Greek*, *history*, *fire*, *calends*, *lyrics*, *tyrants*, *Church*, *dialects*, *aspirations*, though *Grecian noses* & *brows*, *colonnades* & *pediments*, may still be heard of.
>>>

<<<
For

Grecism, grecize, Greco-, &c. spelling see 4, Œ,
===
**Grecism, grecize, Greco-, &c.** For spelling see Æ, Œ.
>>>

